    },
    "textualMarkers": "none",
    "containmentLimit": null,
    "source": {
      "kind": "original"
    },
    "authoredAt": "2026-08-25",
    "note": "The obvious first move once an attacker knows provenance is inherited: add hops until somebody stops walking. Quoting is a particularly good disguise because a quote is, by construction, a faithful copy - which is exactly what makes it carry the taint intact."
  },
