      "containment": "NEEDS_DECLASSIFICATION",
      "requiredReasons": [
        "taint_exceeds_ceiling",
        "egress_with_tainted_input"
      ],
      "rationale": "a display label built for humans is not a value cleared for machines"
    },
    "textualMarkers": "none",
    "containmentLimit": null,
    "source": {
      "kind": "original"
    },
    "authoredAt": "2026-08-25",
    "note": "The word 'safe' in 'safe display label' is doing dishonest work, and an engineer is likely to believe it. A label is safe TO RENDER - escaped, truncated, stripped of control characters. None of that makes it safe to USE as an argument, and the escaping that made it renderable says nothing about who chose the address inside it."
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": 1,
