    "textualMarkers": "none",
    "containmentLimit": null,
    "source": {
      "kind": "original"
    },
    "authoredAt": "2026-08-25",
    "note": "The attacker holds a genuinely valid signature from a genuinely trusted key and tries to spend it somewhere it was never meant to go. The structural narrowing does the work: admitAttestedToolOutput refuses to MINT for any capability with a real effect or full egress, so the receipt does not exist to be misused. A design that minted it and checked the purpose later would be one forgotten check away from a bypass."
  },
